From: Veron
Subject: [PATCH] cc_macro: an include producing no tokens must not crash

read_all_tokens returns NULL for a file with no tokens in it -- an empty
header, or one holding only comments -- and the splice that follows then walks
last_token->next from a null pointer. Two lines reproduce it:

    : > empty.h
    printf '#include "empty.h"\nint main(){return 0;}\n' > t.c
    M2-Planet --expand-includes -I . -f t.c      ->  Segmentation fault

Nothing to splice means nothing to do, so return.

Found while making .github/workflows/m2-normal-mode-gap.yml stub out the
headers tcc needs and M2libc lacks: the first stub it created crashed the
compiler. It is also the likeliest explanation for the rc=139 this probe
recorded against tccdbg.c and tccelf.c in an earlier run.

NOT the doubly-included-guarded-header case, which was checked and is fine:
the tokens are read and the conditional logic drops them afterwards, so
read_all_tokens still returns a list.

VERIFIED: M2-Planet's output over its own nine source files is byte-identical
with and without this patch.

--- a/cc_macro.c
+++ b/cc_macro.c
@@ -713,6 +713,17 @@
 	struct token_list* new_token_list = read_all_tokens(f, NULL, buffer);
 	new_token_list = reverse_list(new_token_list);
 
+	/* AN INCLUDE THAT PRODUCES NO TOKENS IS NOT AN ERROR, AND MUST NOT CRASH.
+	 * An empty header -- or one holding nothing but comments -- makes
+	 * read_all_tokens return NULL, and the splice below then walks
+	 * last_token->next from a null pointer. Two lines of C reproduce it:
+	 *     : > empty.h ; printf '#include "empty.h"\nint main(){return 0;}\n'
+	 * segfaults. Nothing to splice means nothing to do. */
+	if(NULL == new_token_list)
+	{
+		return;
+	}
+
 	struct token_list* last_token = new_token_list;
 	while(last_token->next != NULL)
 	{
